{
  "title": "ShipJS: Zero to Deploy",
  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "m1",
      "title": "JS Fundamentals",
      "description": "Variables, functions, arrays. Ship your first function.",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "id": "m1l1",
          "title": "Console.log",
          "type": "lesson",
          "fileName": "hello.js",
          "xp": 20,
          "docs": "<p>Use <code>console.log()</code> to print to the console. This is your first shipping tool.</p><p><strong>Task:</strong> Log the string <code>\"I ship\"</code></p>",
          "starterCode": "// Log \"I ship\" to the console\n",
          "solution": "console.log(\"I ship\");",
          "hints": [
            "Use console.log() with parentheses",
            "Put your string in quotes inside the parentheses",
            "The exact string is \"I ship\""
          ],
          "tests": [
            {
              "name": "Logs 'I ship'",
              "type": "log",
              "check": "I ship"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "m1l2",
          "title": "Variables",
          "type": "lesson",
          "fileName": "vars.js",
          "xp": 30,
          "docs": "<p>Declare variables with <code>const</code> and <code>let</code>. Use <code>const</code> by default.</p><p><strong>Task:</strong> Create a const called <code>shipName</code> set to <code>\"ShipJS\"</code> and log it.</p>",
          "starterCode": "// Create shipName and log it\n",
          "solution": "const shipName = \"ShipJS\";\nconsole.log(shipName);",
          "hints": [
            "Use: const shipName = \"ShipJS\";",
            "Then log it with console.log(shipName);",
            "const means the value can't be reassigned"
          ],
          "tests": [
            {
              "name": "Declares shipName with const",
              "type": "regex",
              "check": "const\\s+shipName\\s*=\\s*[\"']ShipJS[\"']"
            },
            {
              "name": "Logs ShipJS",
              "type": "log",
              "check": "ShipJS"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "m1l3",
          "title": "Ship Function",
          "type": "project",
          "fileName": "ship.js",
          "xp": 50,
          "docs": "<p>Functions let you reuse code. Arrow functions are modern JS.</p><p><strong>Task:</strong> Create an arrow function <code>ship</code> that takes a <code>name</code> and returns <code>`Shipping ${name}`</code></p><p>Then call <code>console.log(ship(\"Code\"))</code></p>",
          "starterCode": "// Create ship function and log ship(\"Code\")\n",
          "solution": "const ship = (name) => `Shipping ${name}`;\nconsole.log(ship(\"Code\"));",
          "hints": [
            "Syntax: const ship = (name) => `Shipping ${name}`;",
            "Use backticks for template literals",
            "Don't forget to call console.log(ship(\"Code\"))"
          ],
          "tests": [
            {
              "name": "Defines ship as arrow function",
              "type": "regex",
              "check": "const\\s+ship\\s*=\\s*\\([^)]*\\)\\s*=>"
            },
            {
              "name": "Logs 'Shipping Code'",
              "type": "log",
              "check": "Shipping Code"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m2",
      "title": "DOM & Events",
      "description": "Make pages interactive. Query, listen, update.",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "id": "m2l1",
          "title": "Query Selector",
          "type": "lesson",
          "fileName": "query.js",
          "xp": 40,
          "docs": "<p>Use <code>document.querySelector()</code> to grab elements.</p><p><strong>Task:</strong> In browser console this would work. For this test, just create a function <code>getTitle</code> that returns <code>document.querySelector('h1').textContent</code></p>",
          "starterCode": "// Create getTitle function\n",
          "solution": "const getTitle = () => document.querySelector('h1').textContent;",
          "hints": [
            "Use an arrow function",
            "Return document.querySelector('h1').textContent",
            "Selectors use CSS syntax"
          ],
          "tests": [
            {
              "name": "Defines getTitle function",
              "type": "regex",
              "check": "const\\s+getTitle\\s*=.*=>"
            },
            {
              "name": "Uses querySelector",
              "type": "regex",
              "check": "querySelector\\(['\"]h1['\"]\\)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
